+# Joint difficulty, time and credit qualification contract V1
+
+Status: **research contract; HOLD_NO_GO**. The reviewed listed source is
+`2bb56596e637908c44b5a2ef5984c9c37c7d3cc8`, tree
+`18cfc660131170a5b0c5c7244987a9fcebfb7e62`. The prior PR #835 source,
+`e2a02f9271b49f146e70806c8a66e161b5973971`, retains its historical identity.
+The
+[single development plan](../../../development/TRNM_AI_NATIVE_BLOCKCHAIN_DEVELOPMENT_PLAN.md)
+continues to own implementation order and promotion. This document specifies
+the [qualification reader](../../../../formal/pon-nakamoto-v1/joint_consensus_qualification.py)
+and its [machine contract](../../../../config/pon/joint-consensus-qualification-v1.json).
+It adds no consensus rule, work profile, runtime activation or separate roadmap.
+
+The reader makes the missing joint premises explicit and prevents its V1
+contract from claiming a probability that has not been established. A successful
+inspection says that the reviewed listed source, development parameters,
+conditional components and open obligations agree. It is not a common-prefix
+proof or a native execution receipt. Historical failed observations retain
+their original identities and outcomes.
+
+## 1. Native facts and the exact confirmation event
+
+Both `PNH1/PNP1` and `PGH2/PNP2` owners use the required target derived from
+the selected parent's validated ancestry. Their packet formats and domains
+remain distinct. For an admitted nonzero target,
+
+\[
+w(b)=\left\lfloor\frac{2^{256}}{T_b+1}\right\rfloor.
+\]
+
+The inclusive denominator matters. `T=0` is refused; cumulative credit uses
+checked 512-bit arithmetic. A fully valid candidate replaces the incumbent
+only when its cumulative required credit is strictly greater. A smaller
+winning ticket or advertised peer score does not add credit. Equal credit
+does not replace the current tip.
+
+The installed development settings are spacing 10 seconds, retarget interval
+16, MTP width 11, retarget factor 4 and future skew 120 seconds. These are
+source parameters, not a qualified physical production cadence. The branch's
+upper median and observed-clock upper bound do not certify elapsed work.
+The [joint audit](JOINT_CONSENSUS_DAA_AUDIT_20261108.md) preserves the exact
+integer retarget and timestamp analysis. Its finite observations do not
+establish economic advantage, a resource share or a network failure probability.
+
+For inclusion block `b` and observed active tip `c`, the current confirmation
+implementations in [PNH1 storage](../../../../trillionnium/crates/trnm-pon-node/src/store.rs)
+and [PGH2 confirmation](../../../../trillionnium/crates/trnm-pon-node/src/store/growth/confirmation.rs)
+require verified membership and **both** thresholds:
+
+\[
+\operatorname{height}(c)-\operatorname{height}(b)\geq6,
+\qquad S(c)-S(b)\geq6w(b).
+\]
+
+Depth counts successors, excluding `b`. The credit difference also excludes
+`b`, and the multiplier uses the included block's required work. Six
+successors alone can therefore be insufficient when targets change. An
+observation remains reorganization-sensitive and carries `finalized=false`
+and `execution_authority=false`. No numerical security interpretation of
+these thresholds is supplied by V1.
+
+## 2. Listed source binding and inspection limits
+
+The machine contract contains exactly **23 SHA-256 source pins**. The roster
+is fixed in the reader; omission, addition or changed bytes requires review.
+Their canonical map also has a separately fixed digest in the checker,
+`c142b6758d90e01e1960dc5f7fb110209fa9fd40c25fca22f4010acbc085a459`,
+verified against the listed Git blobs at the reviewed commit. Editing source
+and JSON hashes together still fails that anchor. A new anchor requires a
+reviewed checker change; there is no automatic repinning option.
+
+The preceding PR #835 map digest,
+`f043830de62972528c8464f02e26a2fad21cb9dd40d6b2067ed565b7275e7877`,
+is retained here as a historical identifier, not an accepted alternate anchor.
+The successor keeps the same 23 source paths, eighteen unknown parameters,
+thirteen open obligations, sixteen unknown cost points, null probability
+bounds and false qualification flags. The explicit old/unknown revision
+control remains separate from byte-digest checks. Updating this mapping
+does not rerun native code or transfer a historical execution receipt.
+
+| Group | Count | Reviewed scope |
+| --- | ---: | --- |
+| Project and configuration | 5 | Project boundary, mainline, selected protocol, devnet parameters and work profile |
+| Native package context | 3 | Cargo lock, Node manifest and Node library root |
+| Native consensus and owners | 7 | Consensus arithmetic, PNH1 store, PGH2 store, confirmation, recovery, profile and checked-work paths |
+| Wire and work relation | 3 | PNH1 wire, PGH2 wire and native W1 relation |
+| Conditional relation/cost composition | 5 | Mandatory units, work oracle, contract wire, fixed-probability reader and its JSON contract |
+
+The reader checks strict JSON shape and types, the exact source roster,
+digests, actual devnet values and activation flags, reviewed semantic labels,
+unknown parameters,
+property metrics and the complete thirteen-obligation roster. Duplicate keys,
+noninteger/nonfinite JSON numbers and unsupported claim promotions are errors.
+It uses bounded regular-file reads, then checks the listed files and manifest
+again after composing the cost audit.
+
+This identifies the bytes inspected. It does not authenticate their operator,
+prove the semantic summary, establish an atomic snapshot against a privileged
+concurrent writer, identify a loaded executable, or cover all dependencies and
+entry points. `source_binding_scope` explicitly says
+`listed-files-only-not-build-or-runtime-closure`; native execution and full
+build-closure flags remain false. The report also keeps formal semantic
+verification and current repository ancestry verification false. Equality of these pins is narrower than
+equality of complete branches or release binaries.
+
+## 3. One joint environment, with eighteen unresolved parameters
+
+Each unresolved parameter remains `null`. Null does not mean zero cost,
+independent events, an empty private inventory, a trusted clock or positive
+honest participation. Different security properties cannot select incompatible
+favorable environments.
+
+| Group | Unknowns that must be jointly justified |
+| --- | --- |
+| Resources: five | Physical units and scalarization; all-algorithm classical and quantum lower envelopes; joint initial help/preprocessing/residual state; cross-fork batching, caching and unpublished work |
+| Participation: four | Qualified honest production lower tail; complete adversarial credit upper tail; variation/churn bounds; bootstrap currentness and entry debt |
+| Delivery: three | Complete validated eligible delivery delay; availability, queue, verification and state-service capacity; stale-parent and retention bounds |
+| Clocks: three | Wall-clock skew/drift; wall/monotonic/model-time correspondence; activation, confirmation and recovery coverage |
+| Lifetime: three | Horizon and adaptive starts; initial private inventory; joint environment and cryptographic failure budget |
+
+Resources include failed, cancelled, unpublished and restarted work. A measured
+implementation supplies observations about that implementation; it does not
+establish a lower bound over all legal strategies. Delivery must cover complete
+data and verification, not only a network round trip. Header timestamps,
+observed wall time and analysis time have separate roles.
+
+The [dynamic-participation component](DYNAMIC_PARTICIPATION_V1.md) tracks
+declared bootstrap, qualified generations, entry/carryover debt and departure
+obligations in a finite model. Leaving, cancelling or rejoining does not erase
+already charged tasks. Its records are declarations, not native attestations;
+finite trace consistency does not prove honest production tails, clock truth,
+full-view validity or a native dynamic-fork reduction.
+
+## 4. Security properties remain separate
+
+| Property | Required meaning and present boundary |
+| --- | --- |
+| Common prefix | Retention of confirmed prefixes across qualified honest views, epochs, adaptive confirmation starts and restarts; native reduction unproved and failure bound null |
+| Chain growth | Fully validated, eligible required credit per declared model-time window; positive minimum rate and failure bound unknown |
+| Chain quality | Honest required-credit fraction in sufficiently large stable segments; minimum share and failure bound unknown |
+| Block-count quality | Honest block fraction; not derived automatically from credit quality |
+| Business liveness | Eligible honest transaction inclusion and actual service; not derived automatically from credit growth |
+
+Growth in a credit scalar alone does not ensure useful transactions are
+included or that their effects execute. Weighted quality is not count quality
+when block weights differ. Common prefix requires a native failure-to-tail
+mapping, including honest competing branches and initial inventory; a
+single-node score inequality is only one part of that mapping.
+
+The [native fork mapping](../../../../formal/pon-nakamoto-v1/NATIVE_FORK_MAPPING_V1.md)
+and [work-scale contract](../../../../formal/pon-nakamoto-v1/WORK_SCALE_SECURITY_CONTRACT_V1.md)
+provide conditional reductions. The
+[residual-state contract](../../../../formal/pon-nakamoto-v1/STATEFUL_RESOURCE_TAIL_V1.md)
+retains hidden progress across cuts. The
+[native risk ledger](../../../../formal/pon-nakamoto-v1/NATIVE_RISK_LEDGER_V1.md)
+records claims and expenditure; registration does not prove the submitted
+conditional probabilities. Lifetime composition needs bounds covering every
+relevant start and failure event, without restoring risk allowance on restart.
+
+## 5. Cost calibration does not authorize a score replacement
+
+The [credit-envelope contract](../../../../formal/pon-nakamoto-v1/CREDIT_ENVELOPE_CONTRACT_V1.md)
+already proves that exact scale neutrality for two positive cost functions
+requires their ratio to be constant throughout the competitive range.
+Ideal classical `D` and quantum `sqrt(D)` costs fail that condition on a
+nontrivial range. Its bounded-range compromises solve declared calibration
+problems; they do not prove consensus safety. Taking a square root of each
+block's credit therefore receives no qualification here.
+
+The joint reader reuses the existing
+[fixed-probability cost audit](FIXED_PROBABILITY_COST_CONTRACT_V1.md).
+That audit binds MU1's research probability `1/16` and credit `16u`;
+these are not the installed variable-target W1 chain. All sixteen actual
+classical/quantum cost points remain unproved, with null lower and upper
+bounds. Passing the composed reader supplies no native variable-target cost
+bound and does not register MU1 as an activated work profile.
+
+## 6. Primary results and their transfer boundaries
+
+| Primary source | Relevant result and required boundary |
+| --- | --- |
+| [Garay, Kiayias and Leonardos, variable difficulty, 2019 revision of CRYPTO 2017](https://eprint.iacr.org/2016/1048.pdf) | Dynamic synchronous classical analysis with bounded participation variation and strictly increasing round timestamps; quality is difficulty-weighted. These time semantics differ from native MTP. The authors explicitly say their concentration analysis does not justify Bitcoin's actual epoch parameter. |
+| [Cojocaru et al., Quantum 7:944, 2023](https://quantum-journal.org/papers/q-2023-03-09-944/pdf/) | Fixed-density quantum chain-search bounds and a backbone with classical honest parties. Variable branch targets and W1 physical resource costs require additional reductions. |
+| [Bailey and Sattath, arXiv:2403.08023v2](https://arxiv.org/html/2403.08023v2) | Shows why fixed-difficulty quantum conclusions do not transfer automatically through difficulty adjustment; its ideal search assumptions do not establish W1 hardware costs. |
+| [Garay, Kiayias and Shen, ePrint 2026/1116, revised 2026-09-10](https://eprint.iacr.org/2026/1116) | Official abstract describes constant-time adjustment using parallel chains and approximate agreement. This is a different protocol architecture; the complete revised theorem was not inspected in this continuation. |
+| [Garay et al., variable-difficulty composability, FC 2025](https://eprint.iacr.org/2024/1823) | Simulation-based ledger treatment under participation restrictions; useful for identifying application-composition duties, without certifying the W1/Hepta combination. |
+| [Cao and Guo, arXiv:2312.05506v5](https://arxiv.org/html/2312.05506v5) | Explicit confirmation bounds require independent Poisson mining rates and bounded delivery, with startup/credible-chain conditions. These assumptions cannot be inferred from a configured depth. |
+| [Kiffer et al., CCS 2024](https://www.avivz.net/pubs/2024/nakamoto_capacity.pdf) | Finite communication and verification capacity affect consensus guarantees; bounded network delay alone does not account for service queues. |
+
+## 7. Commands and deliberate refusal
+
+From the repository root:
+
+```bash
+python3 formal/pon-nakamoto-v1/joint_consensus_qualification.py --check
+python3 formal/pon-nakamoto-v1/joint_consensus_qualification.py --require-qualified
+```
+
+`--check` returns **0** only for contract consistency. `--require-qualified`
+returns **3** after that same successful inspection, with
+`REFUSED_UNPROVED_JOINT_CONSENSUS`. Malformed input, changed listed source,
+missing obligations or unsupported claims return **2**. The refusal is an
+expected research result, not permission to weaken checks until they pass.
+
+A valid V1 report retains `qualification=HOLD_NO_GO`,
+`security_probability_calibrated=false`, null CP/CG/CQ, lifetime and
+six-confirmation failure bounds, and false activation, finality and execution
+authority. Future qualification requires a reviewed contract revision and
+evidence verifier for the missing premises; editing JSON numbers or booleans
+cannot supply that proof.
